Geometry deduplication of non-instanced shapes (HDARNOLD_GEOM_DEDUP=2) keeps their own state

In mode 2 (All), identical non-instanced meshes and curves are deduplicated: each duplicate
renders the canonical node through a single-instance Arnold instancer, which overrides the
duplicate's own state per instance. The scene has identical quads, deforming quads and curves
that only differ in what is not hashed for a non-instanced shape:
- transform, including motion-blurred transforms (2 keys, and 3 keys on a curved path), also
  on top of a deforming geometry;
- surface material;
- doubleSided (usd_override_double_sided is off): a single-sided quad facing away is not
  visible, a double-sided one is;
- visibility (invisible prims).

The image must be the same as without deduplication: the usd pass doesn't deduplicate, the
hydra and hydra2 passes do. test_18101 checks the resulting Arnold nodes.

author: sebastien.blaineau.ortega@autodesk.com

PARAMS: {'scene':'test.usda', 'environment':[('HDARNOLD_GEOM_DEDUP','2')]}
